Most election predictors use:
* "<u>tossup</u>": no advantage
* "<u>tilt</u>" (used sometimes): advantage that is not quite as strong as "lean"
* "<u>lean</u>": slight advantage
* "<u>likely" or "favored</u>": significant, but surmountable, advantage (highest ranking given from Fox News)
* "<u>safe" or "solid</u>": near-certain chance of victory

